            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0732" n="633" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg633"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2228: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hendaye</hi></placeName>, [<date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-23T10:00:00+00:00">July 23, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date>]<lb/>[Received 4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>51. Situation here dangerous; battle in the streets quite near the Chancellery
                    yesterday; artillery fire on land and from a small war vessel of the Spanish
                    Government which has already left again. The <pb facs="0733" n="634"
                        xml:id="pg634"/> Popular Front has now won the most of the city, but
                    situation may become still worse if other revolutionary forces arrive here or if
                    the red part of the Popular Front is no longer under control. This telegram has
                    been sent through the courtesy of a French dispatch boat which has just arrived.
                    Impossible to communicate with the Ambassador at Fuenterrabia or with anyone
                    outside of the city. I believe the Americans here are safe up to the present.
                    The British Ambassador is trying to send communication asking for a warship and
                    I recommend that an American ship be sent here immediately if possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
